stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> SIGNAL: IN1 a detector fires on the event backbone, gateway, egress gateway, device receiver or AI edge
    SIGNAL --> CANDIDATE: IN2 candidate opened automatically, evidence attached from India-resident logs, on-call paged
    CANDIDATE --> DISMISSED: IN3 named owner records a false positive with a reason
    CANDIDATE --> TRIAGED: IN4 named owner confirms a real event and sets a class
    TRIAGED --> REPORTABLE: IN5 owner decides the event is reportable under the runbook in section 17.6
    TRIAGED --> NOT_REPORTABLE: IN6 owner records the reasoning and the evidence
    REPORTABLE --> REPORT_STAGED: IN7 report fields pre-staged from system state
    REPORT_STAGED --> REPORTED: IN8 named point of contact files inside the six-hour window
    REPORTED --> FANNED_OUT: IN9 customer notices raised, DPDP breach track opened only once DPDP commences
    FANNED_OUT --> CLOSED: IN10 remediation done and post-incident record written
    NOT_REPORTABLE --> CLOSED: IN11 closure requires the recorded reasoning
    DISMISSED --> [*]
    CLOSED --> [*]

    note right of CANDIDATE
      The six-hour clock starts at awareness,
      not at candidate creation. Every timestamp
      is NTP-synced to NIC or NPL.
    end note

    note right of TRIAGED
      Only a named human classifies. No detector
      and no AI component decides reportability.
    end note
